translated_text:
MAYOR OF SINGKAWANG
WEST KALIMANTAN PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF SINGKAWANG CITY
NUMBER 4 YEAR 2017
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF CHILDREN AND WOMEN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
MAYOR OF SINGKAWANG,

a. that girls as creations of Almighty God need to be protected and their honor, dignity, and self-esteem safeguarded from all forms of discrimination, acts of violence, and exploitation to improve the quality of life of children and women physically, spiritually, and socially in realizing an advanced, just, prosperous, prosperous, and democratic society based on Pancasila and the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

b. that the fate of children and women in Singkawang City needs attention from the Regional Government and society because cases of violence against children and women still occur, and children in conflict with the law, thus requiring efforts to provide legal protection for children and women;

c. that to provide protection for children and women, also as implementation of higher Laws and Regulations and constituting one of the mandatory government affairs that is the authority of the Regional Government, the regulation of protection of children and women needs to be regulated in a Regional Regulation;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Children and Women;

In View of
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 4 Year 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);

3. Law Number 7 Year 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention On the Elimination of All Form of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);

4. Law Number 39 Year 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

5. Law Number 12 Year 2001 concerning Establishment of Singkawang City (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2001 Number 92, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4119);

6. Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 Year 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 Year 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

7. Law Number 23 Year 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

8. Law Number 14 Year 2009 concerning Ratification of Protocol To Prevent, Suppress and Punish Trafficking In Persons, Especially Women and Children, Supplementing the United Nation Convention Against Transnational Organized Crime (Protocol to Prevent, Suppress, and Punish Trafficking in Persons, Especially Women and Children, Supplementing the United Nations Convention Against Transnational Organized Crime) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4990);

9. Law Number 10 Year 2012 concerning Ratification of Optional Protocol to the Convention on the Rights of the Child on the Sale of Children, Child Prostitution and Child Pornography (Optional Protocol to the Convention on the Rights of the Child on the Sale of Children, Child Prostitution and Child Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 149, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5330);

10. Law Number 11 Year 2012 concerning Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

11. Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 Year 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

12. Government Regulation Number 4 Year 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);

13. Government Regulation Number 9 Year 2008 concerning Procedures and Mechanisms for Integrated Services for Witnesses and/or Victims of Criminal Acts of Human Trafficking (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 22, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4818);

14. Presidential Regulation Number 69 Year 2008 concerning Task Force for Prevention and Handling of Criminal Acts of Human Trafficking;

15. Presidential Regulation Number 18 Year 2014 concerning Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children in Social Conflict (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 44);

16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 3 Year 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;

17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 Year 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 446);

18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 Year 2011 concerning National Socio-Cultural Strategy to Realize Gender Equality (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 168);

19. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 Year 2011 concerning Policy for Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 168);

20. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 12 Year 2011 concerning Indicators of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 169);

